# Smart Weather Classification & Recommendation System

## Overview

This project is a Computer Vision system that classifies weather conditions from images using Deep Learning and provides simple recommendations based on the predicted result.

The model takes an image as input, predicts the weather class, and outputs a suitable suggestion (e.g., go out / take precautions).

---

## Features

* Image-based weather classification (8 classes)
* Uses MobileNetV2 with Transfer Learning & Fine-Tuning
* Handles real-world images
* Provides recommendation based on prediction
* Achieves ~86.5% accuracy

---

## Classes

* Cloudy
* Dusty
* Foggy
* Other
* Rainy
* Snowy
* Stormy
* Sunny

---

## Dataset

* Collected from multiple Kaggle datasets
* Merged and cleaned into one dataset
* Final size: ~37,723 images
* Balanced using data augmentation
* Split into:

  * 70% Training
  * 20% Validation
  * 10% Testing

---

## Model

* Base Model: MobileNetV2 (pre-trained on ImageNet)
* Transfer Learning applied
* Fine-Tuning used to improve performance
* Final layer: Softmax for multi-class classification

---

## Results

* Test Accuracy: **86.5%**
* Strong performance on:

  * Dusty
  * Stormy
  * Foggy
* Some confusion between:

  * Cloudy and Sunny

---

## Output

The system provides:

* Predicted weather class
* Confidence score
* Recommendation (e.g., safe to go out / take caution)

---

## Tools & Technologies

* Python
* TensorFlow / Keras
* Google Colab
* Scikit-learn
* Kaggle datasets

---

